@startuml write-path
title US-01: Write Path - Position Ping Ingested

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

collections "OpenSky / AIS\nFeed" as Feed
participant "Ingestion\nPoller" as Poller
queue "Kafka\nadsb.raw / ais.raw" as KafkaRaw
participant "Position\nConsumer" as Consumer
queue "Kafka\nposition.normalized" as KafkaNorm
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
database "TimescaleDB\nposition_history" as TSDB

Feed -> Poller : position ping\n(entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms)
Poller -> KafkaRaw : publish to adsb.raw / ais.raw

note over KafkaRaw
  Decouples poller from consumers.
  Absorbs feed bursts without back-pressure.
  Malformed events are routed to DLQ - not shown here (see US-09).
end note

KafkaRaw -> Consumer : consume raw event (at-least-once)
Consumer -> Consumer : parse and normalise\n(validate fields, convert units)
Consumer -> KafkaNorm : publish to position.normalized

Consumer -> Redis : HSET entity:live:{entity_id}\n{ lat, lon, altitude, timestamp_ms }

note right of Redis
  TTL = SIGNAL_LOSS_THRESHOLD_MS
  Key expiry removes stale entities
  from the map automatically.
end note

Consumer -> TSDB : INSERT INTO position_history\nON CONFLICT (entity_id, timestamp_ms) DO NOTHING

note right of TSDB
  Idempotency key: entity_id + timestamp_ms
  Safe to replay from Kafka offset.
end note

@enduml
